   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The three curves A, B and C shown are the graphs of a function f and its derivatives f' and f''. Identify which curve is the graph of each function.",
      "command_verb": "identify"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "statement",
      "label": "Curve A is the graph of \\( f' \\), curve B is the graph of \\( f \\), and curve C is the graph of \\( f'' \\)."
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Curve B has horizontal tangents at x = 0 and x = 4, and curve A crosses the x-axis at exactly those inputs, changing sign there. So curve A is the derivative of curve B.",
         "rule_named": "zeros of a derivative sit at the turning points of the function"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Curve A has its only turning point at x = 2, where curve C crosses the x-axis. So curve C is the derivative of curve A.",
         "rule_named": "zeros of a derivative sit at the turning points of the function"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The chain runs B, then A, then C, so curve A is the graph of \\( f' \\), curve B is the graph of \\( f \\), and curve C is the graph of \\( f'' \\).",
         "rule_named": "order of differentiation"
      }
   ],
